        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{17}{25}$",
          "worked": "Let $W$ be the event of winning. The two winning cases are mutually exclusive.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(W)&=\\frac{3}{10}\\times\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{7}{10}\\times\\frac{4}{5}\\\\P(W)&=\\frac{3}{25}+\\frac{14}{25}\\\\P(W)&=\\frac{17}{25}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
